{"diagnosis": "Fetch TB reports TRAP: no progress max_addr=0x00000000 and tohost FAIL 0xdead instead of advancing through 256-word NOP mem. Expected decoder_trigger from mem_do_rinst && mem_done at picorv32.v:1446 to advance PC past 0x00000000, but do_waitirq stuck at 1 at picorv32.v:1450 forces permanent WFI wait and blocks fetch. Root cause is default do_waitirq <= 1 should be 0; fixing picorv32.v:1450 restores progress.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -1446,10 +1446,10 @@
 		decoder_trigger <= mem_do_rinst && mem_done;
 		decoder_trigger_q <= decoder_trigger;
 		decoder_pseudo_trigger <= 0;
 		decoder_pseudo_trigger_q <= decoder_pseudo_trigger;
-		do_waitirq <= 1;
+		do_waitirq <= 0;

 		trace_valid <= 0;

 		if (!ENABLE_TRACE)
 			trace_data <= 'bx;
", "expected": "tohost PASS with max_addr advancing beyond 0x00000000 through 256-word NOP mem, no TRAP: no progress"}

